WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
Finding the One Piece is the final step to&nbsp;
become king of the pirates. And with Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.980
Blackbeard, and Shanks all&nbsp;
chasing the legendary treasure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.720
they are guaranteed to eventually clash&nbsp;
before the end of the story. But then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:18.420
wouldn’t it make a ton of sense if the three&nbsp;
strongest pirate captains had one final epic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:24.480
clash 1 vs 1 vs 1 to determine once and for&nbsp;
all who will become king of the pirates.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.740
Which leaves us with a massively&nbsp;
interesting question: What would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.000
happen if Luffy fought Blackbeard&nbsp;
and Shanks for the One Piece.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.100
In this scenario, Luffy and the Straw Hats have&nbsp;
already collected all four Road Poneglyphs. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.060
have just landed on Lodestar island, the&nbsp;
final island in the Grand Line. And you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:47.760
may be wondering why they are here, since&nbsp;
technically Lodestar is optional for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:53.160
Straw Hats. After all, this is the island that a&nbsp;
pirate should first learn about the poneglyphs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:57.360
which are these unbreakable stones that&nbsp;
have information from the Void Century.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.040
And although the Straw Hats do not need&nbsp;
to learn about the poneglyphs, Roadstar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:08.040
island is bound to hold other secrets about the&nbsp;
Void Century and the secrets of the One Piece.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.660
And you might have noticed I have already&nbsp;
called this legendary island both Lodestar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.280
AND Roadstar. And that’s because we don’t&nbsp;
actually know it’s real name. In Japanese&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.680
it is called ロードスター and of course in Japanese&nbsp;
there is no difference between R and L. So just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.960
like for the longest time with Laugh Tale,&nbsp;
there is some confusion about the name. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.900
both names kinda make sense since a Lode stone&nbsp;
is basically a magnet which attracts metal. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:36.480
Roadstar works because you could have different&nbsp;
paths pointing out from the island like a star.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.380
So they’ve landed on this mysterious island,&nbsp;
and even though we don’t actually know what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:46.200
it looks like, I like to imagine it looks&nbsp;
something like this. And boy is Robin in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.940
archeologist heaven as she uncovers the&nbsp;
ancient ruins that dot the island. And at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:55.860
the center of it all is this magnificent temple&nbsp;
that explains the true nature of the Poneglyphs.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:01.260
But while Luffy is bouncing around exploring,&nbsp;
an ear-splitting shriek rips through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:06.000
air. On the beach by the Sunny, Nami was&nbsp;
busy charting the course to Laugh Tale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.960
but now a creeping darkness is eating up the sand.&nbsp;
Nami and Zoro frantically run from the darkness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:18.780
until Zoro suddenly spins around in the blink&nbsp;
of an eye and blocks an invisible attack with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:24.960
his swords. And the sheer force of the clash sends&nbsp;
Nami stumbling right into the creeping darkness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.780
She screams out for help, her voice cracking with&nbsp;
terror, as she is sucked into the black abyss.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.740
And just as Nami is about to fully&nbsp;
disappear into the pitch black darkness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:40.560
Luffy swoops in at the last moment and&nbsp;
yanks her to the safety of higher ground.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.720
Zoro leaps up to join the rest of the crew up&nbsp;
on the cliff, and together they stare down at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:51.180
Blackbeard and his titanic captains. Somehow&nbsp;
the evil Yonko has followed the Straw Hats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.080
which means it is finally time&nbsp;
for their ultimate confrontation.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:00.480
And of course Blackbeard can’t help himself,&nbsp;
so he dives into a dramatic speech about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.640
power of dreams and how it is his destiny to find&nbsp;
the One Piece. However, if blackbeard thought the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:11.640
straw hats would just cower in fear like everyone&nbsp;
else, he was gravely mistaken. And right in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:17.460
middle of his speech, he gets absolutely&nbsp;
crushed by a giant punch from Luffy. And a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:23.220
furious Nami unleashes bolts of lightning while&nbsp;
Franky blasts the enemy crew with laser beams.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.860
The Straw Hats are not messing around.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:33.720
And of course, there are many different ways this&nbsp;
could go down. One option is that Luffy could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:41.400
initially be defeated, as happens in most story&nbsp;
arcs. Or since this is one of THE FINAL BATTLES,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:47.160
Luffy might finally defeat his hated rival on the&nbsp;
first try. And since this clash will undoubtedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:53.280
take place in the main story, I am sure that the&nbsp;
godly version that Oda creates will blow all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.280 --> 00:04:00.360
our minds. But that doesn’t mean we can’t have fun&nbsp;
imagining how this epic battle could go. And if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:06.600
you thought Marineford was tragic, just wait until&nbsp;
you see what happens at the end of this video.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:12.780
But one thing that is certain is these two&nbsp;
crews have been set up to fight from the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:19.200
first time that we meet Blackbeard. Both crews&nbsp;
have the same basic roles such as Navigator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:24.840
Swordsman, Doctor, Helmsman, and so on.&nbsp;
Plus, Blackbeard is the main reason that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:31.560
Luffy’s brother Ace was killed, so, trust me,&nbsp;
there is plenty of motivation for this fight.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.900
So the crew leaps down onto the shore to protect&nbsp;
the Sunny and forces the Blackbeard pirates to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.180
retreat. Van Auger, the sniper of Blackbeard’s&nbsp;
crew, uses his teleportation devil fruit to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:46.920
take all of the crew deeper into the island and&nbsp;
away from the Straw Hat’s onslaught. The Straw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:52.440
Hats immediately give chase, with only Jinbe&nbsp;
and Brook staying behind to protect the ship.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:58.260
And this is when the fight breaks up&nbsp;
into specific match ups. And while we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:08.820
don’t know for sure how these fights would&nbsp;
go, we can reasonably guess based on what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.800
we know about the characters from the&nbsp;
story. Of course, the one match up that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:19.920
is guaranteed is Luffy versus Blackbeard.&nbsp;
The ultimate clash of the darkness versus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:25.080
the sun. And this fateful battle begins in&nbsp;
the heart of the ancient temple. Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:31.200
immediately pulls Luffy in with his darkness&nbsp;
gravity, but Luffy’s crazy speed, strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:37.920
and insane haki prove too much for Blackbeard,&nbsp;
and Luffy deals a devastating first blow.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:43.740
Elsewhere around the island, Zoro and the&nbsp;
swordsman Shiryu are carving a path through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:49.860
the forest. Even though Shiryu can turn&nbsp;
invisible, Zoro’s observation haki allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:56.460
him to sense the former jailer’s attacks, and the&nbsp;
pair exchange devastating slashes. Up in the sky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:02.460
Nami and Chopper are flying on Nami’s pet cloud&nbsp;
Zeus as they fight the crazy Doc Q. And this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:09.480
sickly doctor unleashes bursts of horrifying&nbsp;
illness over the entire island, but Chopper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:15.780
uses his medical expertise to counteract the&nbsp;
plagues. On this side of the island, Franky is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:21.960
engaged in an epic wrestling match with the Buff&nbsp;
fruit user, Jesus Burgess. That leaves Sanji and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:27.120
Robin to team up against the shape-shifting&nbsp;
Caterina Devon, the liquor fruit user Doc Q,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:33.420
and the island fruit user Avalo Pizarro. And&nbsp;
of course we have the godly duel of snipers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:40.080
with Usopp and Van Auger literally attempt&nbsp;
to snipe each other from across the island.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:47.940
And at this point, you might be wondering&nbsp;
about the former admiral Aokiji, who joined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:52.800
Blackbeard’s crew during the time skip. But&nbsp;
personally I don’t believe he will remain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:59.160
with Blackbeard’s crew by the end of the story,&nbsp;
so for this video let’s assume he is no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:04.620
part of the crew. Likewise, it is possible that&nbsp;
Blackbeard eventually gains a third devil fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:09.780
but for this video we will assume he only&nbsp;
has the darkness and the tremor fruit.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:15.600
But as the epic battle continues, let’s&nbsp;
recap the goals of each crew. The straw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:20.880
hats already have the Road Poneglyphs, and Nami&nbsp;
already knows where to go to find Laugh Tale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:25.620
so really there is no reason they&nbsp;
have to stay. But Luffy and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:30.180
others surely want revenge for all the pain&nbsp;
Blackbeard has caused them in the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:36.960
so for now they are fighting for their pride&nbsp;
and to stop a rival from finding the One Piece.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:42.600
But the Blackbeard pirates actually do&nbsp;
need the copies of the Road Poneglyphs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.740
So by taking out the Straw Hats,&nbsp;
they will have everything they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:50.340
need to reach Laugh Tale and for&nbsp;
Blackbeard to become pirate king.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:57.660
But back to the battle. Blackbeard is not going to&nbsp;
be king of anything because he is being pummeled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:05.820
by Luffy. Combining the imaginative powers of&nbsp;
Gear 5 and his advanced haki, Luffy delivers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:25.260
blow after blow to his rival. Now Luffy&nbsp;
charges up for one final massive punch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:30.480
but as his fist connects with Blackbeard’s&nbsp;
face, Luffy is shocked when he is pulled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:35.220
into Blackbeard’s darkness. Blackbeard&nbsp;
grabs Luffy’s arm, and, because of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:40.140
special powers of the darkness fruit, Luffy&nbsp;
immediately loses his devil fruit powers.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:48.540
Now Blackbeard has taken a lot of damage,&nbsp;
but he still spreads his gap-toothed grin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:54.900
because he has Luffy trapped. Enraged, Luffy&nbsp;
throws his head back to slam into Blackbeard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.900 --> 00:09:00.000
but before he lands the blow,&nbsp;
Blackbeard ABSOLUTELY CRUSHES&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.400
Luffy with an earthquake-infused punch&nbsp;
that literally shakes the entire island.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:10.980
But Luffy doesn’t stay down for long. He rises&nbsp;
from a crater in the center of the temple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:18.180
bleeding, and his legs wobbling. Still, he keeps&nbsp;
his own defiant smile on his face. What else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:24.600
could we expect in this battle of legendary&nbsp;
D clan? However, one of these captains will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.540
certainly not be smiling at the end of&nbsp;
this video. Keep watching to find out who.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:33.180
Now you might have noticed that we haven’t yet&nbsp;
mentioned some of the Blackbeard crew members. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:39.360
this guy is kind of hard to miss. San Juan Wolf,&nbsp;
the giant fruit user, is walking in the ocean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:45.600
toward the Thousand Sunny. And as we showed in&nbsp;
a recent video comparing sizes in One Piece, San&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:51.300
Juan Wolf can make himself more than three times&nbsp;
the size of the Straw Hat’s ship. So together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:58.560
Brook and Jinbe begin an all out assault against&nbsp;
the enormous man. And although he is super sized,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:04.560
he actually is weakened by the effects of&nbsp;
the sea so this fight is pretty even for now.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:10.500
And back around the island, Nami and Chopper&nbsp;
have managed to defeat Doc Q. They waste no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:15.720
time in going to assist Sanji and Robin, but,&nbsp;
just as they reach their crewmates, the island&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:22.440
literally explodes, sending boulders hurtling&nbsp;
through the air. Sanji and Robin are thrown into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:28.740
the sky like ragdolls. Good thing both of them can&nbsp;
basically fly, but as they regain their balance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:36.000
a giant face appears from the ground. Pizarro has&nbsp;
used the ridiculous powers of his devil fruit to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:42.060
merged with the island and is now launching&nbsp;
giant chunks of rock at the straw hat crew.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:48.900
Zoro sees what is happening and rushes over to&nbsp;
help the crew. Sanji takes over fighting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:54.660
invisible swordsman, getting revenge for missing&nbsp;
out on his favorite devil fruit. And just like he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.660 --> 00:11:01.740
did in Dressrosa, Zoro begins slicing up parts of&nbsp;
the island to try to take out Pizarro’s main body.

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:05.460
Meanwhile, Franky simply cannot&nbsp;
match the raw strength of Burgess,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:06.720
and is his pinned to the ground.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:12.960
But back on the shore, ALL HELL has broken loose.&nbsp;
With the massive San Juan Wolf threatening to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:19.140
crush the Sunny, Brook and Jinbe are going all&nbsp;
out to protect the ship. But this leaves the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:24.480
Sunny unprotected, and now the unthinkable&nbsp;
occurs. Rising from the deck of the ship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:32.880
the angel winged Laffitte flies away with every&nbsp;
copy of the Road Poneglyphs. And that’s it. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.600
Blackbeard crew has accomplished their main goal&nbsp;
and now they just need to— *pauseomentarily*

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:43.080
In a flash of black and red, an air-splitting&nbsp;
slash slices through Laffitte’s wing. With his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:48.000
severed wing flapping uselessly, he falls&nbsp;
towards the ground like a rock. And so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:54.960
do the Poneglyph rubbings. Until… they are&nbsp;
caught by a one armed man in a badass cape.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:56.760
Shanks has arrived.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.440
And you won’t believe how the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:02.700
arrival of the Red Hair Pirates will&nbsp;
change the outcome of this battle.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:07.200
Without warning, the Red Hair&nbsp;
pirates burst into the fray,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:12.240
demanding that you subscribe to the channel.&nbsp;
Shanks leaves the precious poneglyphs on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:17.940
ship and then leaps to the temple. Luffy&nbsp;
and Blackbeard sense his awesome power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:23.280
approaching and it takes a combined effort&nbsp;
to block a wicked sword slash from Shanks.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:32.400
And Luffy is utterly confused, but Shanks&nbsp;
isn’t messing around. He delivers a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:38.280
punch to Blackbeard that sends the evil captain&nbsp;
flying across the temple. Amd then he nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:43.440
cuts off Luffy’s leg. While Luffy dodges, he&nbsp;
falls to the ground with his head spinning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:48.660
And Shanks sieves the opportunity to snatch&nbsp;
the treasured straw hat from Luffy’s head.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:52.620
Stunned, Luffy can do nothing&nbsp;
but watch as Shanks smiles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:59.220
and places the hat upon his own head. He looks&nbsp;
at Luffy and says, “I’ll be taking this back.”

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:04.500
And this causes Luffy to literally&nbsp;
lose his mind. This is his first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:09.540
seeing his former hero in over twelve&nbsp;
years. It should be a happy moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:14.880
but instead Shanks attacks him again.&nbsp;
With confused anger, Luffy strikes back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:20.160
and their overwhelming conqueror’s haki&nbsp;
reduces the temple all around them into rubble.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:24.060
And it is at this point that we have&nbsp;
to acknowledge that Shanks is deadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:28.080
serious about this fight. In the manga,&nbsp;
it was revealed that Shanks definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:32.400
intends to find the One Piece, so while&nbsp;
we don’t know his true motivations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:37.740
he clearly intends to take the copies of&nbsp;
the Poneglyphs in order to reach Laugh Tale.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:43.680
And we don’t know exactly how strong&nbsp;
Shanks and his crew are compared to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:48.420
everyone else. But from the way they&nbsp;
have been portrayed in the story so far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:52.740
I personally think that they are&nbsp;
the strongest crew in the story.

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:59.220
And this becomes obvious right away.&nbsp;
Usopp’s father Yasopp instantly snipes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:02.520
Van Auger, clipping his hat with&nbsp;
a bullet from across the island.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:08.100
Lucky Roux, this bowling ball of a&nbsp;
man, smashes into Burgess and Franky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:11.040
sending the two crashing into the ruins.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:17.100
And the others join in, attacking both the&nbsp;
Blackbeard and Straw Hat crews. In fact, just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:22.500
like how the Straw Hats and Blackbeard’s crew are&nbsp;
set up with similar roles, Shanks’ crew basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:29.100
is the same. Hongo is the doctor. Bonk Punch and&nbsp;
Monster are the musicians. Building Snake is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:34.800
navigator, so there are a lot of possibilities&nbsp;
for match ups between the three crews. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:41.460
the combined power in this potenital fight is&nbsp;
the most insane thing we will see in the stor

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:45.480
And needing the regroup, the Straw Hats&nbsp;
decide to pull together. Remember they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:51.180
don’t actually need the poneglyphs, since&nbsp;
Nami already knows where Laugh Tale is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:56.580
but they also don’t want Blackbeard of Shanks&nbsp;
to have them. So while the rest of the crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:02.820
pulls back towards the Sunny, Zoro and Sanji&nbsp;
attack the Red Hair ship, intending to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:12.540
back the poneglyph rubbings. But that is no easy&nbsp;
task. They are met by Shanks’ right hand man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:17.400
Ben Beckman, and Howling Gab, who manage&nbsp;
to keep the Straw Hats off of the ship.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.840
And with the battle spilling onto the&nbsp;
beach, Pizarro appears to try to crush&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:28.020
the enemy crews with a giant sand fist,&nbsp;
but this turns all the attention onto him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:34.560
and every sword user in the Straw Hat and Red&nbsp;
Hair crew attack at once, absolutely destroying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:39.720
the island man. Defeated, Pizarro falls&nbsp;
unconscious in a bloody heap on the beach.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:44.940
Back to the captains, Shanks is finally&nbsp;
getting revenge for Blackbeard scaring his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:50.940
face all those years ago. The Red Hair captain&nbsp;
is relentless with his legendary sword skills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:55.500
unleashing attacks with the full&nbsp;
force of the absolute strongest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.500 --> 00:16:01.140
haki in the series. Blackbeard is forced&nbsp;
to defend with his tremor coated fists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:08.280
but he is struggling. As is Luffy. While Luffy&nbsp;
can block Shanks’ blade with advanced Conqueror’s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:14.700
Shanks isn’t giving him any openings to attack&nbsp;
because his future sight is slightly superior.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:19.920
But with Shanks and Luffy momentarily&nbsp;
distracted with each other, Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:26.580
decides that this is a battle he would rather&nbsp;
not fight. He calls for Van Auger and the sniper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:32.160
teleports in and just as quickly teleports&nbsp;
his captain back to the beach. Luffy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:38.400
Shanks clash a bit more, but then they both&nbsp;
sense something dangerous from the shore.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:44.700
Although San Juan Wolf is weakened by the&nbsp;
water, he is still incredibly massive. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:53.700
he spreads his arms, closes his eyes, and begins&nbsp;
a massive belly flop onto the ships. The Straw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:59.460
Hats and Red Hair crew focus all of their&nbsp;
attacks on him, but they simply cannot stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:04.920
the massive figure from falling. But then,&nbsp;
right before the giant crushes the ships,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:10.920
Shanks and Luffy appear. And with a&nbsp;
blistering haki-filled fist and sword slash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:16.740
they absolutely destroy the giant and&nbsp;
send him flying across the island.

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:20.100
That’s one obstacle down. And many more to go.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:25.680
But before Luffy can confront Shanks, his former&nbsp;
mentor disappears again. And down on the beach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:32.940
Robin shouts at Luffy, recommending that they flee&nbsp;
the battle. Again, they don’t need to be here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:37.920
and the only thing they risk here is being&nbsp;
defeated. So despite his desire to fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:43.260
Luffy makes the wise choice to signal&nbsp;
the retreat. But before Robin can move,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:49.080
Shanks appears behind her, grabs her by&nbsp;
the hair and puts his blade to her throat.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:53.340
Damn. This is not going to end well for someone.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:18:00.900
And at this point it is important to remember that&nbsp;
Robin is the only one here who is confirmed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:05.820
able to read the poneglyphs. Blackbeard&nbsp;
did capture Big Mom’s daughter, Pudding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:09.540
and she might be able to read them if&nbsp;
she awakened her third eye abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:14.580
but that is uncertain. So even&nbsp;
though Shanks has the Poneglyphs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:20.460
he would still need someone to read them.&nbsp;
Which explains why he would kidnap her.

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:25.800
Luffy screams in rage. If there is one&nbsp;
thing that drives Luffy to the edge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:30.960
it is his friends being hurt. We’ve&nbsp;
seen it in Arlong Park, Enies Lobby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:37.380
and especially Sabaody. So if they are in&nbsp;
danger, Luffy will do anything to take her back.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:44.100
Now Sanji tries to stop Shanks, but the&nbsp;
Red Hair captain dashes away with Robin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:51.360
Luffy tries to follow Shanks and Robin, but is&nbsp;
stopped by Jesus Burgess. After a few moments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:56.040
Luffy tosses Burgess aside, and then finds&nbsp;
Shanks clashing with Blackbeard near the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:56.040 --> 00:19:02.880
waves. But Robin is nowhere in sight. As we can&nbsp;
all imagine, Luffy is furious. And so while he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:09.120
may have been subconsciously holding back against&nbsp;
his former friend, he now unleashes his full fury&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:15.480
against Shanks. And Shanks is slightly distracted&nbsp;
by Blackbeard, so he senses Luffy’s attack late.&nbsp;

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:19.680
And this momentary slip has&nbsp;
devastating consequences.

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:26.160
Luffy pummels Shanks into the ground, spewing&nbsp;
sand and water into the air. Luffy unleashes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:31.080
a storm of punches until Ben Beckman&nbsp;
attacks Luffy from the side. Luffy dodges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:37.560
but it allows Shanks to rise to his feet.&nbsp;
He is shaken from the attack. Blood drips&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:43.560
down his face. His eyes are unfocused. He&nbsp;
raises his sword. But then, he freezes.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:48.780
Blood spurts from his mouth. He looks down.&nbsp;
Three blades stick out from his chest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:53.580
and then from behind Shanks, a sickening laugh&nbsp;
breaks the breathless silence of the beach.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:20:00.900
Blackbeard withdraws his three knives,&nbsp;
standing over Shanks as he falls to the ground.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:06.480
Luffy is stunned. Tears form&nbsp;
in his eyes. Conqueror’s haki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:12.840
erupts in overwhelming bursts of rage and&nbsp;
sadness, shaking the island. His mentor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:18.900
his friend, is dying in front of him.&nbsp;
He cannot handle it. His eyes tremble.

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:23.760
But then another shriek rips across&nbsp;
the island. Near Blackbeard’s ship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:25.920
Robin is struggling against Shanks.

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:30.660
Wait, what? Hold on. Shanks is dying&nbsp;
on the ground. What is going on???

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:37.320
As the second Shanks locks Sea prism on Robin’s&nbsp;
wrist, his form changes. And the shape-shifting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:42.900
Caterina Devon laughs as she holds up the&nbsp;
weakened Robin. The rest of the straw hats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:47.760
rush to help Robin, but they are held back&nbsp;
by the Blackbeard crew. The Red Hair pirates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:53.940
circle around to help Shanks, but Hongo simply&nbsp;
shakes his head. There is nothing he can do.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.740
Shanks is dying.

00:20:55.740 --> 00:21:01.320
And with his last ounce of strength, he points&nbsp;
at Luffy. The trembling Luffy steps forward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:06.120
barely able to move, and he falls&nbsp;
to his knees. The rage is gone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:12.780
and now only tears remain. Luffy says that is&nbsp;
sorry. Over and over again he repeats it through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:17.940
his tears. But Shanks shakes his head and says&nbsp;
that if he cannot get to the One Piece himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:22.380
then it is Luffy’s responsibility&nbsp;
to find it before Blackbeard does.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:27.240
So with his dying breath, Shanks orders&nbsp;
his crew to stop Blackbeard and help Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:34.440
escape. Then he places the straw hat back on&nbsp;
Luffy’s head. And the light in his eyes fades.

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:39.240
While holding back tears, the Red Hair pirates&nbsp;
stand. No matter the sadness they feel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:44.340
they will follow their captain’s last command.&nbsp;
So they take the fight to the Blackbeard crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:50.640
seeking vengeance for their fallen captain.&nbsp;
Luffy joins in, smashing everything while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:55.440
crying out in his grief. Eventually,&nbsp;
they rescue Robin and the crew pulls back

00:21:55.440 --> 00:22:03.180
But Luffy cannot control himself. He was tricked&nbsp;
and it cost Shanks his life. So he is desperate to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:03.180 --> 00:22:09.660
keep fighting, and it takes the combined efforts&nbsp;
of Zoro and Nami to bring him away from the fight.

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:16.500
So the Red Hair pirates hold off Blackbeard&nbsp;
and his crew. The Straw Hats, including the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:22.080
badly injured Franky, have just enough time to&nbsp;
board the Sunny and escape into the stormy seas.

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:27.060
And next there is only one place to&nbsp;
go. Laugh Tale. But it will not be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:27.060 --> 00:22:30.720
simple for the Straw Hats to get there,&nbsp;
because Blackbeard would undoubtedly be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:35.640
chasing him all the way. And on top of that the&nbsp;
marines will certainly redouble the efforts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:35.640 --> 00:22:39.780
stop Luffy from finding the One Piece and&nbsp;
the ancient secrets of the void century.

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:46.440
And with the straw hats weak from this insane&nbsp;
battle, there may not be a better chance for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:46.440 --> 00:22:52.320
marines to do just that. Can you imagine Akainu&nbsp;
swooping in and taking out the straw hats right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:52.320 --> 00:22:54.720
after Shanks died? And even MORE interesting&nbsp;
scenario could be what if the marines actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:00.480
managed to capture Luffy? What would the rest of&nbsp;
the crew do? And who would come to save him? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:05.940
if you’re curious to learn how that might&nbsp;
play out, you can watch this video right here.

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:07.436
Shanks for watching.

